config MT7601U
	tristate "MediaTek MT7601U (USB) support"
	depends on MAC80211
	depends on USB
	help
	  This adds support for MT7601U-based USB wireless dongles.

config MT7601U_RESEARCH
	bool "MT7601U research / experimental features (raw TX, RF test, MAC-rand, CSI probe)"
	depends on MT7601U
	default n
	help
	  Compile the surface-A research feature set into the mt7601u driver:
	  raw packet injection from a monitor vif, RF/baseband test modes
	  (continuous-TX / single-tone -- these EMIT a carrier on 2.4 GHz and are
	  LAB / SHIELDED-CHAMBER ONLY, subject to RF regulation), silent-capture
	  (auto-ACK disable), fast MAC randomization, and the CSI-feasibility
	  BBP-block-dump probe. All are exposed via debugfs / module params and
	  are for RF bring-up and security research, NOT normal operation.

	  If unsure, say N. The fleet production kernel MUST keep this N so the
	  emitting / spoofing / raw-TX surface is not compiled into shipped images.
